			"date": "2025-11-13T16:44:06.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> you must be a good person.</p><p>i’ve seen there’s also “disqualification”, when the person or system giving feedback wants to play, consciously or not, the zero-sum status game. i assume you add it to criticism and take the best out of it, which is a great strategy.</p><p>but knowing that in the world there’s both malice and people that play games, can help one make better decisions on who to, and who not to, look for feedback from.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
