			},
			"date": "2025-11-13T16:58:34.291Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@argonaut\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>argonaut</span></a></span> huh — yeah, I’ve seen that. I would say that no matter how successful you are, folks will find a way to disqualify you (if they want).</p><p>I would also just add one small little thing that I cringe a little bit when I hear someone qualified as “good” — good or bad is how we participate in a thing at a small scale, in the choices we make</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115543587973915752",
			"parentId": "115543448898192834",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@argonaut/115543587918062004",
			"author": {
				"name": "argonaut",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@argonaut",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/852/910/290/536/965/original/f26330025ff9163f.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2025-11-13T17:33:55.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> totally agree, i don’t see value in categorising as good or bad, i see value in what takes you closer or farther from what you expect, want, desire, search for, etc. </p><p>value judgements are always points of view and they move with strategy changes, popular opinion, overton windows… so usually of little valuable use.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
